/-!
# Exceptional-carrier generation for the terminal seed

All four exceptional branches are proved for their literal carriers: A₆, A₇,
the nonsplit hexacode triple cover, and the derived octonion model of G₂(2).
Each leaf establishes the intrinsic Sylow-overgroup property for every Sylow
subgroup and every overgroup, including the whole group. The proofs use
subgroup orders for A₆, checked cubic words for A₇, cubic lifting through the
actual cover map, and derived Bruhat coverage for G₂(2)′.

`Application` connects all four branches to the original quotient seed and
discharges the exceptional premises of the existing binary-model adapters.
The intrinsic leaves remain independent of the parent `MarkedSeed` import;
the all-model assembly retains the separate binary linear branch and the
earlier-source inputs.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), 15.3.49(l)
and its point-stabilizer applications, printed pp.1144–1145.
-/
